# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MAIL STORES ARE NEVER COMMITTED.
#
# This is the first rule in the file because it is the one whose failure is
# irreversible: a PST is somebody's correspondence, and a public repository
# that has ever held one has published it, `git rm` notwithstanding.
#
# Every `.pst`/`.ost` is ignored. Exactly ONE file is exempted, by name:
# tests/fixtures/Empty.pst, which is Microsoft's own MIT-licensed empty store
# from the upstream Rust repository (see NOTICE) and contains no mail.
#
# scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit enforces this a second time, because a
# `git add -f` silently defeats everything above. Install it: scripts/setup.sh
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pst
*.ost
*.pab
!tests/fixtures/Empty.pst
# The public corpus: every file here is licensed, synthetic-or-vendor test
# data, and SHA-256 pinned in tests/fixtures/public/MANIFEST.sha256. The hook
# and CI refuse any .pst whose hash is not in that manifest. ADR-0004.
!tests/fixtures/public/*.pst

# Private fixtures — real mail, used locally, never shared.
tests/fixtures/private/

# The upstream Rust source. Fetched, never vendored: scripts/get_rust_source.sh
# Both spellings: `reference/` matches the directory, `/reference` also matches
# the symlink the orchestrator plants in each row worktree.
reference/
/reference

# Rust build output, wherever cargo lands it
target/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
build/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Oracle capture output (differential-testing scratch, regenerable)
.oracle-cache/

# CodeGraph local index
.codegraph/

# rtk upstream checkout, if the rtk skill is bootstrapped here
.claude/skills/rtk/upstream/

# Per-row agent worktrees (docs/AGENTS.md). Branches live in .git; the dirs are scratch.
.worktrees/
